## 🎉 Rotating Card – Hover‑to‑Rotate (CSS Only)

Below is a **complete, ready‑to‑copy** example that shows how to create a card that flips (rotates) when you hover over it.  
It uses only **HTML + CSS** – no JavaScript needed.

> **Tip:**  
> - `perspective` gives the 3‑D effect.  
> - `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps the inner faces in 3‑D space.  
> - `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the backside when it’s turned away.  
> - `transition` makes the flip smooth.

---

### 📄 HTML

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <!-- Front side -->
    <div class="card-face front">
      <h2>Front</h2>
      <p>To jest karta frontowa.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Back side -->
    <div class="card-face back">
      <h2>Back</h2>
      <p>To jest karta tylna.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

---

### 🎨 CSS (`style.css`)

```css
/* 1️⃣ Global reset (optional but handy) */
*,
*::before,
*::after {
  box-sizing: border-box;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
}

/* 2️⃣ Center the card on the page */
body {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  min-height: 100vh;
  background: #f0f0f0;
  font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
}

/* 3️⃣ Wrapper gives perspective */
.card-wrapper {
  perspective: 1000px;          /* How far the viewer is from the card */
}

/* 4️⃣ The card itself */
.card {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;  /* Keep children in 3‑D space */
  transition: transform 0.8s ease; /* Smooth flip */
}

/* 5️⃣ Hover → rotate the card */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);   /* Flip around Y‑axis */
}

/* 6️⃣ Common face styles */
.card-face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden; /* Hide backside when turned away */
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  color: #fff;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  text-align: center;
  padding: 20px;
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
}

/* 7️⃣ Front side */
.front {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff6b6b, #f06595);
}

/* 8️⃣ Back side – rotate 180° so it starts hidden */
.back {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #4a90e2, #50e3c2);
  transform: rotateY(180deg);   /* Start flipped */
}
```

---

### 🔍 How It Works

| Step | What Happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| 1 | Reset margins/padding | Keeps layout predictable |
| 2 | Center the card | Makes demo look nice |
| 3 | `perspective` | Gives depth to the 3‑D effect |
| 4 | `transform-style: preserve-3d` | Keeps child elements in 3‑D space |
| 5 | `transition` | Smooth animation |
| 6 | `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the backside when it’s turned away |
| 7 | `.front` | Front face styling |
| 8 | `.back` + `rotateY(180deg)` | Back face starts flipped, so it becomes visible when the card rotates |

---

### 🎯 Customization Ideas

| Feature | How to tweak |
|---------|--------------|
| **Flip direction** | Change `rotateY(180deg)` to `rotateX(180deg)` for vertical flip |
| **Speed** | Adjust `0.8s` in `transition` |
| **Perspective distance** | Increase/decrease `perspective` value |
| **Card size** | Change `width`/`height` of `.card` |
| **Colors** | Replace gradients with solid colors or images |
| **Content** | Add images, icons, or more complex layouts inside `.card-face` |

---

